## Non-Goals

- Do not silently or automatically apply any Skill update.
- Do not run `git pull`, `git reset`, `git clean`, discard local commits, or
  overwrite a dirty/ahead checkout.
- Do not refresh a plugin marketplace during audit or treat marketplace refresh,
  Codex CLI update, symlink discovery, or an upstream release as proof that the
  effective installed Skill changed.
- Do not force unsafe remove/reinstall behavior for a channel that lacks a
  deterministic atomic apply and rollback adapter.
- Version 1 keeps Codex plugin replacement audit/diagnostic-plan-only with no
  actionable `plan-id` and returns a channel-mutation blocker. Git-backed
  plan/apply may materialize only the exact
  temporary or immutable candidate named by that action inside its bound
  candidate/release roots; it may not initialize or mutate a sibling source,
  live checkout, or other user repository.
- Do not install `mattpocock/skills` or alter Scheme C's selected workflow
  architecture.
- Do not make the updater a required Router dependency, add it to the Router
  portable cross-CLI manifest, or modify Antigravity/Grok runtimes.
- Version 1 does not implement controller self-apply; it reports
  `BLOCKED_SELF_UPDATE` and a Router-owned fixed-source deployment resume
  condition.
- Do not synchronize credentials, tokens, sessions, history, logs, caches,
  hooks, settings, binaries, private keys, or other runtime-owned sensitive
  state.
- Do not infer authorization for `git init` in a sibling/source/live target,
  staging, commit, branch/tag/remote mutation, reset, clean, push, PR, release,
  plugin installation, or publication. A fixed, disclosed Git candidate
  materialization is authorized only by its plan request or exact apply
  approval and grants none of those repository/publication operations. The
  sole repository-reference exception is the exact user-approved task 2.1
  creation of the disclosed local `add-codex-skill-update-v2` branch and
  replacement worktree; it grants no mutation of the quarantined prior
  `add-codex-skill-update` ref/worktree/admin path and no staging, commit,
  remote, push, PR, release, or publication.

